Feature: Agent Log Calculated Field Extraction and Population in purgo_playground.agent_log

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the source tables are "session_tracking_data", "user_presence_tracker", and "agent_profile_data"
    And the target table is "agent_log"
    And the following hardcoded values are used:
      | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code |
      | New York   | NY          | USA           | 10001          |
    And the hashing algorithm for agent_key is "MD5"
    And the current timestamp is used for "data_loaded_at"

  # Happy Path: All required data present and valid
  Scenario: Populate agent_log with calculated fields for a valid agent session
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | "A123"           | "2025-01-15 08:00:00"   | "2025-01-15 17:00:00"   |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | "A123"           | "agent1@company.com"   |
    And agent_profile_data contains records with
      | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | "agent1@company.com"  | "IU_001"         | "John Smith"   | "2025-01-14 12:00:00"    |
      | "agent1@company.com"  | "IU_002"         | "John S."      | "2025-01-15 09:00:00"    |
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id  | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | "IU_002" | "John S."  | "2025-01-15"| "2025-01-15 08:00:00" | "2025-01-15 17:00:00"  | "9.0"                | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | <current_timestamp>    | <md5_hash_value>  |

  # Data-driven: Multiple sessions per agent per day
  Scenario Outline: Calculate first login, last logout, and total login time for multiple sessions
    Given session_tracking_data contains records for agent "<person_identifier>" on "<log_date>"
      | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | <first_login>          | <first_logout>          |
      | <other_login>          | <other_logout>          |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | <person_identifier> | <email_address>      |
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with
      | email_address     | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | <email_address>   | <internal_user_key> | <full_name> | <last_modified_timestamp> |
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id            | agent_name     | log_date      | agent_first_login | agent_first_logout | total_login_time_hrs |
      | <internal_user_key>| <full_name>    | <log_date>    | <first_login>     | <first_logout>     | <duration_hrs>       |

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | log_date    | first_login           | first_logout           | other_login           | other_logout           | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp | duration_hrs |
      | "A124"           | "2025-01-16"| "2025-01-16 07:45:00" | "2025-01-16 18:00:00"  | "2025-01-16 12:00:00" | "2025-01-16 13:00:00"  | "agent2@company.com" | "IU_003"         | "Jane Doe"     | "2025-01-16 10:00:00"   | "10.25"      |
      | "A125"           | "2025-01-17"| "2025-01-17 09:00:00" | "2025-01-17 17:30:00"  | "2025-01-17 14:00:00" | "2025-01-17 15:00:00"  | "agent3@company.com" | "IU_004"         | "Bob Lee"      | "2025-01-17 09:30:00"   | "8.5"        |

  # Error Scenario: Missing session_end_time
  Scenario: Handle missing session_end_time for an agent
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time |
      | "A126"           | "2025-01-18 08:00:00"   | NULL            |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | "A126"           | "agent4@company.com"   |
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with
      | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | "agent4@company.com"  | "IU_005"         | "Alice Wong"   | "2025-01-18 08:00:00"    |
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id  | agent_name   | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | "IU_005" | "Alice Wong" | "2025-01-18"| "2025-01-18 08:00:00" | NULL               | NULL                 | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | <current_timestamp>    | <md5_hash_value>  |

  # Error Scenario: Missing agent_profile_data for email
  Scenario: Handle missing agent_profile_data for email_address
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | "A127"           | "2025-01-19 09:00:00"   | "2025-01-19 17:00:00"  |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | "A127"           | "agent5@company.com"   |
    And agent_profile_data does not contain a record for email_address "agent5@company.com"
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | NULL    | NULL       | "2025-01-19"| "2025-01-19 09:00:00" | "2025-01-19 17:00:00"  | "8.0"                | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | <current_timestamp>    | <md5_hash_value>  |

  # Error Scenario: Missing user_presence_tracker for person_identifier
  Scenario: Handle missing user_presence_tracker for person_identifier
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | "A128"           | "2025-01-20 10:00:00"   | "2025-01-20 18:00:00"  |
    And user_presence_tracker does not contain a record for person_identifier "A128"
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | NULL    | NULL       | "2025-01-20"| "2025-01-20 10:00:00" | "2025-01-20 18:00:00"  | "8.0"                | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | <current_timestamp>    | <md5_hash_value>  |

  # Validation: Field formats and rules
  Scenario Outline: Validate field formats and error conditions
    Given agent_log is populated for agent "<agent_name>" with
      | unix_id  | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | <unix_id>| <log_date>  | <agent_first_login>   | <agent_first_logout>   | <total_login_time_hrs>| <agent_city>| <agent_state>| <agent_country>| <agent_zip_code>| <data_loaded_at>      | <agent_key>       |
    When the record is validated
    Then unix_id should be a string or NULL
    And agent_name should be a string or NULL
    And log_date should be in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    And agent_first_login and agent_first_logout should be in "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" format or NULL
    And total_login_time_hrs should be a string representing decimal hours or NULL
    And agent_city should be "New York"
    And agent_state should be "NY"
    And agent_country should be "USA"
    And agent_zip_code should be "10001"
    And data_loaded_at should be a valid timestamp
    And agent_key should be a valid MD5 hash string

    Examples:
      | unix_id  | agent_name   | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key         |
      | "IU_006" | "Sam Green"  | "2025-01-21"| "2025-01-21 08:30:00" | "2025-01-21 17:30:00"  | "9.0"                | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | "2025-01-21 18:00:00"  | "d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e" |
      | NULL     | NULL         | "2025-01-22"| "2025-01-22 09:00:00" | NULL                   | NULL                 | "New York" | "NY"        | "USA"         | "10001"        | "2025-01-22 18:00:00"  | "d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e" |

  # Error Scenario: No session_tracking_data for a given day
  Scenario: No agent_log record created when no session_tracking_data exists for a day
    Given session_tracking_data does not contain any record for log_date "2025-01-23"
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then no agent_log record should exist for log_date "2025-01-23"

  # Error Scenario: Multiple agent_profile_data records for same email, select most recent
  Scenario: Select most recent agent_profile_data for duplicate email_address
    Given agent_profile_data contains records for email_address "agent7@company.com"
      | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | "IU_007"          | "Tom Hardy"    | "2025-01-24 09:00:00"    |
      | "IU_008"          | "Thomas Hardy" | "2025-01-24 10:00:00"    |
    And session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | "A129"           | "2025-01-24 08:00:00"   | "2025-01-24 17:00:00"  |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | "A129"           | "agent7@company.com"   |
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | unix_id  | agent_name     | log_date    | agent_first_login      | agent_first_logout      | total_login_time_hrs |
      | "IU_008" | "Thomas Hardy" | "2025-01-24"| "2025-01-24 08:00:00" | "2025-01-24 17:00:00"  | "9.0"                |

  # Error Scenario: agent_lunch_login, agent_lunch_logout, agent_lunch_duration are not populated
  Scenario: agent_lunch fields remain NULL due to lack of source data
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | "A130"           | "2025-01-25 08:00:00"   | "2025-01-25 17:00:00"  |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | email_address          |
      | "A130"           | "agent8@company.com"   |
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with
      | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | "agent8@company.com"  | "IU_009"         | "Sara Lee"     | "2025-01-25 08:00:00"    |
    When the agent_log is populated
    Then agent_log should have a record with
      | agent_lunch_login | agent_lunch_logout | agent_lunch_duration |
      | NULL              | NULL               | NULL                |
